---
/**
 * About / Our Story — copy from pages-content/_ about - Our Story.docx.
 * Composes shared widgets only. Photos come from the Sanity "About" singleton
 * (`aboutContent`); a missing photo renders the grey placeholder.
 */
import PageLayout from '~/layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import Hero2 from '~/components/widgets/Hero2.astro';
import TextSplit from '~/components/widgets/TextSplit.astro';
import Text from '~/components/ui/Text.astro';
import Button from '~/components/ui/Button.astro';
import { getAboutImages } from '~/lib/content';
import RelatedBlogs from '~/components/widgets/RelatedBlogs.astro';

const images = await getAboutImages();

const metadata = {
  title: 'Our Story | Taqueria El Ranchero in Oʻahu',
  description:
    'Learn about Taqueria El Ranchero’s Northern California taqueria influence, ranchero-style dishes, daily preparation, and two Oʻahu locations.',
  ignoreTitleTemplate: true,
};

const linkClass = 'text-accent underline underline-offset-4 transition-opacity hover:opacity-80';
---

<PageLayout metadata={metadata}>
  {/* ── Hero — Kapolei restaurant exterior ── */}
  <Hero2
    variant="split-dark"
    image={images.hero}
    overlapHeader={false}
    title="About Taqueria El Ranchero"
    content="At Taqueria El Ranchero, we bring Northern California-inspired Mexican taqueria cooking to Oʻahu. Our approach centers on ranchero-style food, fresh daily preparation and meals made for everyday dining.<br /><br />From our original restaurant in Wahiawa to our newer location in Kapolei, we focus on the straightforward cooking that defines our taqueria style."
  />

  {/* ── Our Story ─────────────────────────────────────────── */}
  <TextSplit id="our-story" heading="Our Story">
    <div class="flex flex-col gap-6">
      <Text variant="body-lg" color="default">
        Taqueria El Ranchero takes its inspiration from the Mexican taquerias of Northern California, where familiar
        dishes and simple preparation are central to the experience.
      </Text>
      <Text variant="body" color="default">
        Our first restaurant opened in Wahiawa, serving the surrounding neighborhood and people traveling through
        Central Oʻahu. We later expanded to Kapolei at Ka Makana Aliʻi, bringing the same menu to a full-service dining
        setting.
      </Text>
      <Text variant="body" color="default">
        Today, both restaurants share the same approach to food. Whether you’re visiting our
        <a href="/locations/wahiawa" class={linkClass}>Wahiawa location</a> or dining with us in
        <a href="/locations/kapolei" class={linkClass}>Kapolei</a>, you’ll find the tacos, burritos and ranchero-style
        dishes that define El Ranchero.
      </Text>
    </div>
  </TextSplit>

  {/* ── Ranchero Style ────────────────────────────────────── */}
  <TextSplit id="ranchero-style" heading="Ranchero Style" class="bg-card">
    <div class="flex flex-col gap-6">
      <Text variant="body-lg" color="default">
        The word ranchero refers to ranch-style cooking. For us, that means straightforward meals built around familiar
        ingredients such as chicken, beef, pork, rice and beans.
      </Text>
      <Text variant="body" color="default">
        Our food follows a Northern California taqueria approach rather than Tex-Mex or fusion cooking. We focus on
        recognizable dishes prepared with traditional combinations of meats, vegetables, tortillas and salsa.
      </Text>
      <Text variant="body" color="default">
        That approach runs throughout our menu, from everyday tacos and burritos to our signature
        <a href="/menu/entrees" class={linkClass}>Molcajete</a>, which brings grilled meats and vegetables together in
        a sizzling volcanic stone mortar.
      </Text>
    </div>
  </TextSplit>

  {/* ── Made Fresh Daily — open-fire grill ── */}
  <TextSplit id="made-fresh-daily" heading="Made Fresh Daily" withImage image={images.madeFreshDaily} imageAspect="4 / 3">
    <div class="flex flex-col gap-6">
      <Text variant="body-lg" color="default">Fresh preparation is part of our routine at El Ranchero.</Text>
      <Text variant="body" color="default">
        Each morning, our kitchen teams grill meats over an open-fire grill and prepare fresh vegetables and herbs. Our
        salsas are made in-house, ready to accompany the dishes served throughout the day.
      </Text>
      <Text variant="body" color="default">
        When you place an order, we assemble your food using ingredients prepared earlier that day. This allows us to
        serve tacos, burritos and other menu favorites efficiently while keeping daily preparation at the center of how
        we cook.
      </Text>
    </div>
  </TextSplit>

  {/* ── Local Partners ────────────────────────────────────── */}
  <TextSplit id="local-partners" heading="Local Partners" class="bg-card">
    <div class="flex flex-col gap-6">
      <Text variant="body-lg" color="default">
        Our daily preparation starts with ingredients supplied through local food distributors.
      </Text>
      <Text variant="body" color="default">
        We receive meats through a local distributor and work with a Hawaiʻi produce supplier for vegetables and other
        produce. From there, our kitchen teams prepare the ingredients used in our menu each day.
      </Text>
      <Text variant="body" color="default">
        These supplier relationships support our approach to serving freshly prepared food at both El Ranchero
        locations.
      </Text>
    </div>
  </TextSplit>

  {/* ── The Murals — chalk-art mural (photo still needed from the client) ── */}
  <TextSplit id="the-murals" heading="The Murals" withImage image={images.murals} imageReverse imageAspect="4 / 3">
    <div class="flex flex-col gap-6">
      <Text variant="body-lg" color="default">
        The chalk-art murals at El Ranchero are a visual connection between our two restaurants.
      </Text>
      <Text variant="body" color="default">
        Our Wahiawa location has a rustic, neighborhood taqueria atmosphere, while Kapolei offers a sit-down dining
        experience with table service and outdoor seating. Each restaurant has its own character, but the murals bring
        a recognizable part of El Ranchero into both spaces.
      </Text>
      <Text variant="body" color="default">
        They’re part of the setting guests experience when they visit us for a meal or spend an evening at the
        restaurant.
      </Text>
    </div>
  </TextSplit>

  {/* ── Community gathering place — restaurant interior ── */}
  <TextSplit id="community" heading="A Gathering Place for the Community" withImage image={images.givingBack} imageAspect="4 / 3" class="bg-card">
    <div class="flex flex-col gap-6">
      <Text variant="body-lg" color="default">
        Our connection to Oʻahu goes beyond the food we serve. El Ranchero is also a gathering place for the island’s
        Latino community, with music and events that welcome everyone.
      </Text>
      <Text variant="body" color="default">
        Our regular programming includes karaoke, Latin Night and live concerts featuring Mexican bands. These
        gatherings bring people together around music and shared cultural experiences.
      </Text>
      <Text variant="body" color="default">
        You can explore our <a href="/events" class={linkClass}>weekly events and upcoming performances</a> to see
        what’s happening at El Ranchero.
      </Text>
      <div class="flex flex-col gap-3 pt-2 sm:flex-row">
        <Button variant="primary" text="Explore Our Menu" href="/menu" hideNote={true} />
        <Button variant="ghost" tone="light" text="Find a Location" href="/locations" hideNote={true} />
      </div>
    </div>
  </TextSplit>
  <RelatedBlogs pageSlug="about" surface="grey" />
</PageLayout>
